[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4720063790","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120337#issuecomment-4720063790","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120337","id":4720063790,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGVZ1Lg","user":{"login":"nathancarter","id":1316622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTY2MjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1316622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter","html_url":"https://github.com/nathancarter","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-16T14:48:00Z","updated_at":"2026-06-16T14:48:00Z","body":"In a resolved conversation above, @Mickeon [said](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120337#discussion_r3420550163) the following phrase isn't clear: \"The left and right tangents may be different if the curve is not continuous at this point.\"\r\n\r\nThe goal of the phrase was to explain why a curve might need two tangents at one point, which is something probably unfamiliar to most people coming from a standard math education, in which there is usually only one tangent to a curve at any given point.  In other words, many people may come to this documentation and ask themselves, \"What does left and right tangent even mean?\"  And the documentation doesn't answer that question, so I was attempting to give some hint here.\r\n\r\nIf it's not clear or doesn't fit the project goals, feel free to delete it.  But that's the explanation for why it's there.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4720063790/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4727854542","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120337#issuecomment-4727854542","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120337","id":4727854542,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGc1Vzg","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-17T08:52:35Z","updated_at":"2026-06-17T08:52:35Z","body":"> The goal of the phrase was to explain why a curve might need two tangents at one point\"\r\n> In other words, many people may come to this documentation and ask themselves, \"What does left and right tangent even mean?\"\r\n\r\nIt doesn't really answer this question. If anything it poses _more_ questions:  What does \"continuous\" mean and, most importantly, how does this affect the user? Because the existence of both \"left\" _and_ \"right\" tangents, by itself, implies that they're distinct.\r\n\r\n- For users that **know** what a \"tangent\" is, it's not hard to imagine what \"left tangent\" and \"right tangent\" means.\r\n- For users that **do not know** what a \"tangent\" is, it doesn't matter much, because the meaning becomes clear with the surrounding context, with the way they are used in **Curve**.\r\n\t- By virtue of what **Curve** is, it's relatively easy to understand it manually in the Inspector. When selecting a point, two separate handles appear and they can be modified individually. As far as the user is concerned, that's what the \"left tangent\" and \"right tangent\" are.\r\n\t","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4727854542/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4754146081","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120337#issuecomment-4754146081","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120337","id":4754146081,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG16DIQ","user":{"login":"nathancarter","id":1316622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTY2MjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1316622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter","html_url":"https://github.com/nathancarter","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/gists{/gist_id}","st