"organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-19T19:18:32Z","updated_at":"2026-06-19T19:58:33Z","body":"Mickeon is a documentation maintainer and presents a lot of good arguments, please be respectful of maintainers and their feedback, and if you are not interested in the review process and the requirements for PR approval then it might be best to close this\r\n\r\nThis \"take it or leave it\" attitude is not how you do collaborative development ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4754156318/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4754232141","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120337#issuecomment-4754232141","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120337","id":4754232141,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG1_TTQ","user":{"login":"nathancarter","id":1316622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTY2MjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1316622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter","html_url":"https://github.com/nathancarter","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nathancarter/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-19T19:33:21Z","updated_at":"2026-06-19T19:33:21Z","body":"Let me clarify:\r\n\r\n1. The most important part of the PR is the replacement of the incorrect text \"angle\" with the correct text \"slope.\"  This is not an opinion; it has been an open bug in Godot for 5.5 years (#45117).  It would be silly to delete this part of the RP, especially since nobody (a well respected maintainer or anyone else) is complaining about that part of the PR.\r\n2. The unimportant part of the PR is the exposition I added about left and right tangents.  Since we disagree on what should go in there, let's just delete that part and keep the part we agree on, which is the important part.\r\n\r\nSo it's not a \"take it or leave it\" attitude at all.  I'm not at all saying \"delete the whole PR.\"  I'm saying \"delete the part the maintainer doesn't like so that the important part can go through.\"\r\n\r\nI'm not suggesting anybody is a bad maintainer or isn't representing the community well.  I'm not attempting to disrespect anyone.  However, we seem to have different opinions about what content would be helpful here.  That's okay.  The arguments above don't convince me, and I (not out of anger) don't have any interest in writing a long defense of my opinion.  That's not disrespect, it's just how I choose to use my time.\r\n\r\nSo, like I said above, let's just delete the part you don't like and keep the part we agree on.\r\n\r\nIf you would like me to modify the PR in this way, just say so and I can do it.  Also, I don't mind if someone else does it instead.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"ht